# FortiGate safety

## Read-only default

List devices, policies, addresses, routes, interfaces, and health checks are
fine when FortiGate work is authorized. Do **not**:

- create/update/delete firewall policies
- change NAT / VIP / static routes
- remove address or service objects still referenced by policy

…unless the user gave an explicit verb this turn naming the object (and VDOM
when required).

## Blast radius

ACL/NAT changes can drop management or user traffic. State the risk, prefer
narrow edits, and refuse “open everything” style asks without a clear target.
